################################################################################
# P0-1 — style.css (2 edits)
# Mechanism: calculator-suite.css:111 sets `.calc-tool-hero h1{color:#fff}` for the
# old navy-gradient hero. The 08-30 editorial rollout recolors the hero background to
# cream (--editorial-warm #f3f0e8) via `.calculator-page .calc-tool-hero{...}` but
# never overrides the text color, so the H1 renders white-on-cream at 1.13:1 —
# effectively invisible. Verified live (screenshot + getComputedStyle) on
# calculator-payment, calculator-affordability; calculator-refinance-breakeven has the
# identical class pair. asset-depletion is NOT affected (inline navy background wins).
# Same class of bug as the .lp-trust-chip fix Adam caught on 08-30.
################################################################################

FILE: style.css

FIND:
.calculator-page .calc-tool-hero h1{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin-bottom:.35rem}

REPLACE:
.calculator-page .calc-tool-hero h1{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin-bottom:.35rem;color:var(--color-navy)}

FIND:
.calculator-page .calc-tool-hero p{max-width:700px;margin-bottom:0}

REPLACE:
.calculator-page .calc-tool-hero p{max-width:700px;margin-bottom:0;color:#536172;opacity:1}

# Note: #536172 is the exact subtitle color the editorial system already uses for
# .hero-subtitle on loan/location/trust/guide pages — matches the design system.
# opacity:1 neutralizes calculator-suite.css's `.calc-tool-hero p{opacity:0.9}`.

################################################################################
# P0-2 — rate-buydown-calculator.html (1 edit)
# On-screen schedule header says Principal|Interest at columns 5-6; the row renderer
# emits r.interest then r.principal (L903-904). The full-schedule modal header
# (Interest|Principal) matches the cells and is correct. In month 1, the column
# labeled "Principal" shows the (much larger) interest figure. Swap the two <th>.
################################################################################

FILE: rate-buydown-calculator.html

FIND:
                  <th scope="col">Principal</th>
                  <th scope="col">Interest</th>

REPLACE:
                  <th scope="col">Interest</th>
                  <th scope="col">Principal</th>

################################################################################
